{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire","id":689801,"title":"Freshly turned Vampire","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-05T09:34:24-07:00","id":689801,"title":"<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/icons/icon5.png\" width=\"16\" height=\"16\" alt=\"\" /> Freshly turned Vampire","content":"Last night during game play I came across a situation i wasnt sure how to handle exactly. I know that vampires are &quot;frozen&quot; the way they were when they died so If they had a super bad hair cut or chipped nails or terrible scars or .. whatever. They are stuck like that for eternity... So what exactly happened was a vampire when into a hunger frenzy and violently fed on a loved one. like ripped their throat open and nommed them down.. They were like, &quot;Oh shit. oops! I will turn them..&quot; What happens to the throat? They were dead with a gaping wound... I know you can embrace after death, but are they stuck with that wound for all eternity? I hope they like scarfs...<br /> <br /> <br /> Sort of related question since I am here... The original vampire has nasty scars and I told the player that since I was posting I would ask on it about. He was wondering if the very old scars from human life can be healed in anyway now that he is a vampire. I said no because he is stuck with the time of death, but perhaps there is blood sorcery or something I am unaware of. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T09:44:48-07:00","id":689833,"title":"","content":"I'd say either the wound just becomes a huge scar, or they can heal it with blood but it opens back up every night and has to be re-healed. <br /> <br /> There might theoretically be one way to get rid of a scar, if you're willing to get a bit creative. What they need to do is carve the scarred flesh off with a knife, then heal the damage. Theoretically the new flesh should be unmarked, and they can then spend a willpower when they go to sleep to keep the change.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T13:19:28-07:00","id":690199,"title":"","content":"The vampire's body returns to the state it was in at the time of their death every night. However, I've been told that it is possible for a vampire to heal pre-existing conditions using their vitae. For example, an amputee could spend the blood to regenerate their missing limb (assuming they used to have one), but it would fall off again at the start of each night, forcing them to regrow it each time.<br /> <br /> Vampires are capable of modifying their appearance, it just doesn't last very long unless they're making a continuous effort to maintain it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T13:58:04-07:00","id":690329,"title":"","content":"You can make permanent any changes a vampire does to their body. I believe the cost is a willpower point (not a dot). So if a vampire gets a tattoo, or regenerates a limb I suppose, they can make that change permanent so they don't have to keep doing it.<br /> <br /> Some vampires shave their heads and make that permanent so they can more easily change their hair with wigs, since they can't grow it out.<br /> <br /> As for injuries, I've always just assumed that fresh wounds heal upon the embrace. No evidence for that viewpoint, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1692-maina","name":"Maina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1692_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"724"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-05T23:51:27-07:00","id":690934,"title":"","content":"It also says that becoming a vampire improves their appearance slightly, though in a slightly creepy way. I've always interpreted that to mean that the Beast perfects the host slightly, from its perspective. Meaning it gets rid of injuries, and maybe fixes little things like that hint of a beer-gut, creating a ferally seductive and fully-functional predator. Beyond those minor improvements by the Beast, though, vampires are frozen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T02:06:42-07:00","id":690979,"title":"","content":"I normally also go with the theme that the embrace smoothes over some damage/or health conditions prior to the embrace, either by the sire providing enough vitae with the embrace or just mystically.<br /> <br /> I had a daeva player who made it a theme for her character. before the embrace her character had flaky skin, because of severe neurodermitis, but after the embrace - her character looked &quot;healthier&quot; than before... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Gamelines: Requiem, Lost, Awakening, Trinity Continuum: Aeon, some V5.<br /> Likes cheesecake (quark-based)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1305-maekkel","name":"maekkel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1305_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"206"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T02:29:53-07:00","id":690986,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, anyone embraced is going to have a track full of lethal or worse, so if it the embrace can fix <i>that</i> then I supposed a little thing like a slashed throat should be no trouble.<br /> <br /> Really though, Requiem vampires are not nearly as static in appearance as those in Masquerade. I mean, a few weeks ago we were discussing the possibility of a vampire growing their hair out with repeated uses of the blush of life and willpower in another thread.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T07:58:39-07:00","id":691268,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the input everyone. I appreciate it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T11:05:49-07:00","id":691443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=690329#post690329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for injuries, I've always just assumed that fresh wounds heal upon the embrace. No evidence for that viewpoint, though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I don't know- the Embrace is a pretty... <i>turbulent </i>event, with all sorts of potential to go wrong. Personally I would have thought that if those kinds of wounds didn't heal, then they'd be a LOT more prevalent.<br /> <br /> ...pretty flimsy and circumstantial, but it's something <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T11:44:23-07:00","id":691475,"title":"","content":"Well, considering the Embrace was basically a post-frenzy afterthought, i would say that combined with the scar could result in her returning as a larva or revenant instead of true kindred - of course, supposing either possibility exists in one's game and that it would be interesting for the story and group, of course.<br /> <br /> As a kindred, if the sire didn't arrange for some blood source to help out with &quot;weaning&quot; and healing its newly embraced childe, the throat staying as a gaping wound is pretty probable, possibly requiring vitae spending every night just to be able to feed effectively (or not - if kindred do not really digest the blood in the stomach or even breath, why would the throat affect the spread of vitae through their bodies - let's be honest, kindred physiology is weird and pretty much a mystery).<br /> <br /> At least until she learns enough of how a kindred's body works to maybe heal the throat (as usual) and <b>then</b> spend a dot of willpower to make the change permanent (supposing that's still kosher by Requiem's rules), scarring or clean healing being completely optional.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T12:11:26-07:00","id":691545,"title":"","content":"@Baaldam: The requirements to turn into a full kindred were completed. Drain the victim dry, feed the victim and pay the humanity. Since it was an accident, there were no preperations, no food source for the newly turned vampire. <br /> <br /> @hastur00. I agree, which is why I made an executive decision to let the wounds scar over. These wounds severely impair the vampire's ability to speak. I based my decision on the fact that having vampires running around with freakish open wounds that dont bleed until they blush would be a huge masquerade breech. <br /> <br /> It was great to hear the different perspectives; that the beast fixes the corpses upon embrace. It was not something that I had thought of before. I have always sort of assumed that a planned embrace just drained the victim's blood, they lick the wound to remove the evidence, then they feed the corpse, creating a perfect vampire. Even though they are at full lethal there is no external damage to show. I am torn on wether or not vitae can heal *old* scars, like human days scars, There is no evidence or ruling to support one way or the other. I hadnt thought of being able to regenerate a limb that was removed when you were human or that annoying bullet scar. it makes for interesting concepts. I would have thought that blood sorcery or some other weird thing would have to do it other than a pure force of will to make the change. Still torn, so I am going in circles, but I do want to say that I appreciate your thoughts and Ideas!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-06T14:51:12-07:00","id":691731,"title":"","content":"Tzigane Dvorzsak (<b>Ancient Mysteries</b>, p. 94) is an example of a vampire with an unhealing wound from before the embrace. She is missing one eye and covers her left empty eyesocket with a patch. I guess that if it were possible, she would have already healed her eye back.<br /> <br /> But I agree that most books don't take cases of unhealing pre-embrace damage into account, so one example does not mean that it is consistently a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T08:12:51-07:00","id":698628,"title":"","content":"This actually ties in with something I wondered recently - if vamps can spend willpower to make changes to their body permanent, could I, as a self-preservation conscious vamp who's had more than one run-in with Taskforce: VALKYRIE hunters armed with Hod rounds, have a piece of kevlar cut to order and implant it under my rib cage then spend a point of willpower so that my body doesn't reject it while healing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T12:23:58-07:00","id":698866,"title":"","content":"That's up to your storyteller. I can understand wanting kevlar hidden under your ribcage as it auto downgrades bullets from lethal to bashing, but why would you NOT want your character to be able to automatically eject a stake from their body?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T13:49:49-07:00","id":698939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=698866#post698866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's up to your storyteller. I can understand wanting kevlar hidden under your ribcage as it auto downgrades bullets from lethal to bashing, but why would you NOT want your character to be able to automatically eject a stake from their body?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I rather thought the point was to keep them out of there in the first place :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-12T17:36:38-07:00","id":699235,"title":"","content":"Ideally yes. Under normal circumstances, vampires can automatically expel them from their body as they heal. Since you specifically referenced bullets that function as a wooden stake if they're shot in the heart, if the kevlar vest is permanently inserted inside the vampire, they wouldn't be able to expel them, so they're stuck with magical wooden splinters in their body that function as a wooden stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5466,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","user":"tsusasi","date":". 10-12-2015, 08:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T00:56:07-07:00","id":699545,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure how it would stop them coming out if it failed to stop them going in. <br /> <br /> Also I've never heard of vampires being able to expel stuff like that anyway. I think it would rather defeat the point of a stake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T02:24:03-07:00","id":699560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=699545#post699545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how it would stop them coming out if it failed to stop them going in</div> </div> </div> </div>Because<br /> 1. The game mechanics don't accurately simulate how firearms or kevlar works. Instead of actually absorbing and dispersing the kinetic energy of a bullet midflight, kevlar just downgrades the damage intensity. The smallest caliber bullets rip through kevlar when enough dice are thrown. <br /> 2. In order for a bullet to pierce through kevlar in the first place (again depending on the caliber and power of the firearm used) it has to travel over 840 mph. A vampire who's body is pushing out a foreign substance is unlikely to generate the amount of force required to expel it.<br /> <br /> &lt;&lt; Also I've never heard of vampires being able to expel stuff like that anyway. I think it would rather defeat the point of a stake. &gt;&gt;<br /> <br /> I've never heard of vampires in a single setting being able to do half the crap they can do by default in this game line in the first place. How else would a vampire expel foreign objects in their body as it returns to factory defaults? And we aren't talking about stakes, we're talking about magical bullets being allowed to magically immobilize a vampire just as if he had been staked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T04:10:30-07:00","id":699568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=699560#post699560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The game mechanics don't accurately simulate how firearms or kevlar works. Instead of actually absorbing and dispersing the kinetic energy of a bullet midflight, kevlar just downgrades the damage intensity. The smallest caliber bullets rip through kevlar when enough dice are thrown.</div> </div> </div> </div>Armour does both now, actually. And lethal damage doesn't necessarily mean the bullet went in. It also applies to broken bones and other serious trauma. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>tsusasi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=699560#post699560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In order for a bullet to pierce through kevlar in the first place (again depending on the caliber and power of the firearm used) it has to travel over 840 mph. A vampire who's body is pushing out a foreign substance is unlikely to generate the amount of force required to expel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, they would, because the bullet lost all that kinetic energy going through the kevlar. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T04:46:45-07:00","id":699573,"title":"","content":"The... umm.. the vampire's body doesn't need to shoot the bullet out with the same force as it came in...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T09:39:15-07:00","id":699897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=699545#post699545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure how it would stop them coming out if it failed to stop them going in.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ever stuck your hand through bars and realized it got stuck when you tried to pull it out? Or put a ring on that you couldnt get off? Or the videos where people stick their head in something, like between bars, and cant get them out? Things dont come out the same way they come in. especially a bullet or a splintered wood...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=699545#post699545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also I've never heard of vampires being able to expel stuff like that anyway. I think it would rather defeat the point of a stake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> My thoughts on the stake thing... It would make it far less of a scary thing if they just heal the stake and force it out. I very much think that it just heals around the stake, leaving it in. Same as a bullet. if it sinks into them and they heal.. i think it's still there, like a human with a bullet lodged inside them. It's not like wolfman regeneration. I have always pictured it as just sealing up the wound and thats that. A stake automatically sends you into torpor and once there I am pretty sure you cant choose to suddenly heal. I think you heal at dawn. If a stake wasnt a dangerous weapon, meaning you can just heal the stake out and be fine next round, then why mention it drops you into torpor at all?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2308,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","user":"Vitalis","date":". 10-13-2015, 12:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T10:03:39-07:00","id":699916,"title":"","content":"Stakes stop the healing. But I think kevlar wouldn't completely stop the stake, it would just apply an armor bonus against attempts to stake the heart.<br /> <br /> It might just be a Masquerade thing but I'd swear Requiem had a version of the 'take out my heart and store it someplace safe' ability, which grants immunity to staking attempts through the chest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T10:08:24-07:00","id":699921,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=699573#post699573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The... umm.. the vampire's body doesn't need to shoot the bullet out with the same force as it came in...</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to pass through the kevlar the vampire hypothetically installed around its rib cage in the event he's successfully shot with Hod rounds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5466-tsusasi","name":"tsusasi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5466_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T10:27:57-07:00","id":699930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=699916#post699916\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stakes stop the healing. But I think kevlar wouldn't completely stop the stake, it would just apply an armor bonus against attempts to stake the heart.<br /> <br /> It might just be a Masquerade thing but I'd swear Requiem had a version of the 'take out my heart and store it someplace safe' ability, which grants immunity to staking attempts through the chest.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I think there is a Blood sorcery thing you can do for a night to keep you from getting staked.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2308-vitalis","name":"Vitalis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2308_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"914"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-13T10:41:28-07:00","id":699935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vitalis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=699930#post699930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think there is a Blood sorcery thing you can do for a night to keep you from getting staked.</div> </div> </div> </div>There is, but that's not what I'm talking about.<br /> <br /> The Ordo Dracul have it, with the name Surgical Heart Removal. It's a Scale of the Wyrm.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T09:57:06-07:00","id":702278,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Random_Interrupt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=698628#post698628\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This actually ties in with something I wondered recently - if vamps can spend willpower to make changes to their body permanent, could I, as a self-preservation conscious vamp who's had more than one run-in with Taskforce: VALKYRIE hunters armed with Hod rounds, have a piece of kevlar cut to order and implant it under my rib cage then spend a point of willpower so that my body doesn't reject it while healing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, R1 had the specific stipulation that with Willpower, you could heal whatever you wanted, and leave untouched whatever you wanted, when you healed a wound- the specific example given was a grievous injury that had had the skin alone healed to disguise its presence.<br /> <br /> Unless it's been changed, .that's a pretty good precedent. I personally would allow it, but only at the cost of carrying around a balance- and thematically-appropriate amount of bashing damage, accompanied by some Resolve+Medicine rolls, maybe, to reflect the fact that you've got a gaping subdermal wound that's been stuffed with a big scratchy wad of ballistic cloth, then barely healed shut.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1289-hastur00","name":"Hastur00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1289_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T16:43:18-07:00","id":702616,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Hastur00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/689801-freshly-turned-vampire?p=702278#post702278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, R1 had the specific stipulation that with Willpower, you could heal whatever you wanted, and leave untouched whatever you wanted, when you healed a wound- the specific example given was a grievous injury that had had the skin alone healed to disguise its presence.<br /> <br /> Unless it's been changed, .that's a pretty good precedent. I personally would allow it, but only at the cost of carrying around a balance- and thematically-appropriate amount of bashing damage, accompanied by some Resolve+Medicine rolls, maybe, to reflect the fact that you've got a gaping subdermal wound that's been stuffed with a big scratchy wad of ballistic cloth, then barely healed shut.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Nice, that seems a reasonable way of handling it, cheers!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8485-random_interrupt","name":"Random_Interrupt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8485_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"39"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}